  "result": "Default arg `[]` evaluated once, at `def` time. Same list object reused every call.\n\n```python\nadd.__defaults__  # ([1, 2],) after two calls\n```\n\n- `add(1)`: appends to shared list -> `[1]`\n- `add(2)`: appends to same list -> `[1, 2]`\n\nFix: default to `None`, make new list per call.\n\n```python\ndef add(x, items=None):\n    if items is None:\n        items = []\n    items.append(x)\n    return items\n```\n\nNow `add(1)` -> `[1]`, `add(2)` -> `[2]`.",
